(i) $T = v_{1}\cdots v_{5}$ (Proposition \claimref{standard-model.majorana-element}) is a product of five anticommuting nilpotent creators, so $T^{2} = 0$ and $(T^{\dagger})^{2} = 0$. On the module $T$ sends the empty state to the filled state and kills every other basis state, and $T^{\dagger}$ does the reverse, so $T^{\dagger}T$ is the projector on the empty state and $TT^{\dagger}$ the projector on the filled state; hence $TT^{\dagger}T = T$ and $T^{\dagger}TT^{\dagger} = T^{\dagger}$, and every product of two of $T, T^{\dagger}, TT^{\dagger}, T^{\dagger}T$ is $0$ or one of them, so with $1$ they span the algebra generated by $T$ and $T^{\dagger}$. A mass form $B(\psi, X\varphi)$ on the sixteen (the even states) is nonzero only if $X$ sends an even state to a state whose complement is even, that is to an odd state, since the pairing of Lemma \claimref{standard-model.invariant-pairing-five-modes} pairs a state with its complement and five is odd. $w_{4}T$ and $w_{4}T^{\dagger}$ are even, so they give no form; $w_{4}TT^{\dagger}$ and $v_{4}TT^{\dagger}$ vanish on the sixteen (the filled state is odd); $w_{4}T^{\dagger}T$ vanishes because $w_{4}$ kills the empty state. The one survivor is $v_{4}T^{\dagger}T$, which sends the empty state $
u^{c}$ to $v_{4}$ applied to it, paired with the state with the three pair modes and the second rung mode filled: one entry, so its symmetric part is half the $10$ form's neutrino entry and it has an equal antisymmetric part, with no quark entry. \emph{Computed:} the five relations, the closure of the products, the vanishing forms and the $v_{4}T^{\dagger}T$ form. By linearity every element of the algebra gives $w_{4}$ the multiple of the $10$ form carried by its scalar part. The Georgi-Jarlskog form is not a multiple of the $10$ form (computed), so no such element gives it; the stored square results (Proposition \claimref{synthesis.georgi-jarlskog-square-of-majorana-element} and Theorem \claimref{synthesis.georgi-jarlskog-is-rung-vector-times-pair-part-of-majorana-square}) obtain it from $P_{4}$, the pair-only degree-four part of the expansion of $TT^{\dagger}$ in Majorana monomials, a projection of that expansion which is not an operator function of $T$ (the full degree-four part $G_{4}$, and $TT^{\dagger}$ itself, give no symmetric form, Theorem \claimref{synthesis.georgi-jarlskog-is-rung-vector-times-pair-part-of-majorana-square}(iv), computed again here for $TT^{\dagger}$).

